\chapter{Roadmap}

\section{Stage 1 --- the walking skeleton}

The thinnest slice that runs end to end and proves the architecture: open two
accounts, post one balanced transaction between them, print both balances,
and show that an \emph{unbalanced} transaction is refused. It touches every
concept thinly --- Accounts (open, apply, balance), Ledger (post, invariant),
Api (the demo main) --- so when it builds green the shape is proven and
everything after is thickening.

\section{Later stages (planned)}

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Stage 2 --- Reporting}: a trial balance and per-account
    statements over the ledger. New concept \texttt{Reporting}, depending on
    Ledger and Accounts.
  \item \textbf{Stage 3 --- Persistence}: an append-only journal on disk so
    balances survive a restart.
\end{itemize}

\section{The concept ledger}

The single source of truth for what exists and what is planned. Lifecycle:
\texttt{planned $\rightarrow$ stubbed $\rightarrow$ implemented $\rightarrow$
stable}.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{lllll}
\toprule
Concept & Status & Depends on & Stage & Chapter \\
\midrule
Accounts  & implemented & ---              & 1 & \ref{chap:accounts} \\
Ledger    & implemented & Accounts         & 1 & \ref{chap:ledger} \\
Api       & implemented & Ledger, Accounts & 1 & \ref{chap:api} \\
Reporting & planned     & Ledger, Accounts & 2 & --- \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\section{Seam contracts}

The chunks at the boundaries between concepts, named so no one improvises an
interface. In Stage 1 they are filled immediately by the concept chapters:

\begin{description}
  \item[\texttt{Accounts: header}] the account type and the balance-changing
    operations every other concept is allowed to call.
  \item[\texttt{Ledger: header}] the \texttt{Entry} type and
    \texttt{ledger\_post}, the only door through which balances change in a
    transaction.
  \item[\texttt{Accounts: demo accounts} / \texttt{Ledger: demo posting}]
    seed snippets each concept owns and Api composes into the walking
    skeleton.
\end{description}
